and are we headed in the right direction,

785
00:36:06,880 --> 00:36:10,600
especially as more TradFi people come on chains,

786
00:36:10,600 --> 00:36:12,880
more payments move to stablecoins?

787
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:15,280
A lot of people, DeFi purists,

788
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:18,480
even will stick their noses up at stablecoins sometimes

789
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:23,040
as USDC may be on Ethereum, on a decentralized blockchain,

790
00:36:23,040 --> 00:36:26,600
but you're still trusting, circle the company

791
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:31,200
to mint you the USDC and buy and custody

792
00:36:31,200 --> 00:36:33,320
the treasury asset that's underlying it

793
00:36:33,320 --> 00:36:34,520
and redeem it when you ask for it.

794
00:36:34,520 --> 00:36:36,160
There's still a level of trust involved there.

795
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:37,960
So where are we on that spectrum?

796
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:41,120
Are we headed in the right direction in your opinion?

797
00:36:41,120 --> 00:36:43,960
There's a good mix of signals in there, to be honest,

798
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:45,160
but if you zoom out,

799
00:36:45,160 --> 00:36:47,760
I think we are trending in the right direction.

800
00:36:47,760 --> 00:36:50,960
The reason why I say that is just because

801
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:55,040
I've seen TBL start to leave some of these projects

802
00:36:55,040 --> 00:36:57,600
that are in DeFi,

803
00:36:57,600 --> 00:37:00,640
but are reliant on these centralized exchanges

804
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:02,440
or parties or whatever,

805
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:05,200
reducing counterparty risk

806
00:37:05,200 --> 00:37:07,080
and relying on maybe something

807
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,840
that is just a smart contract,

808
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:11,560
getting the human element out of decision-making

809
00:37:11,560 --> 00:37:16,080
will become more popular over time in certain circles.

810
00:37:16,080 --> 00:37:21,080
There's always going to be people who will prefer USDC

811
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:25,960
because it is backed by the government of somewhere

812
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:28,400
or the bank is backed by the government.

813
00:37:28,400 --> 00:37:31,640
I think that that product will always be out there

814
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:33,520
for a good reason too,

815
00:37:33,520 --> 00:37:35,560
at least for Ethereum's vision,

816
00:37:35,560 --> 00:37:39,680
low risk DeFi is a great north star

817
00:37:39,680 --> 00:37:43,400
and that does not involve these centralized entities

818
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:44,880
in that equation at all.

819
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:47,920
It just establishes a base rate of yield.

820
00:37:47,920 --> 00:37:49,840
Even these centralized parties

821
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:52,160
will sometimes fall back on that.

822
00:37:52,160 --> 00:37:57,000
For instance, I think at the peak TBL of Athena,

823
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:02,000
only 30% of their funds were in the carry trade strategy

824
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:04,360
going on between all these centralized exchanges.

825
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:08,000
The rest of it went into Aave to get the Aave yield,

826
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:09,840
which is exactly what we do.

827
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:13,600
You need a base rate of yield

828
00:38:13,600 --> 00:38:15,760
and if it's there and it's robust,

829
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:17,560
can take giant deposits

830
00:38:17,560 --> 00:38:19,600
and people are definitely gonna use it.

831
00:38:19,600 --> 00:38:20,440
That's good.

832
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:22,000
We're moving in the right direction.

833
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:23,040
People are learning.

834
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:24,040
We're educating people.

835
00:38:24,040 --> 00:38:25,680
Maybe that's a good place to leave it.

836
